From 07cf2f391b3cd708ad0bff3dae37dcd1c5e6e2c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:45:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: verisilicon: Crop H.264 encodes to 2 pixel units

The OUTPUT crop rectangle of the encoder is the coded picture size. Its
width is rounded up to a multiple of 4, as the right overfill register
of the H1/VEPU2 counts 4 pixel units, so a 1918 pixel wide picture is
coded 1920 wide and userspace that asked for 1918 can't encode it.

H.264 crops in units of 2 samples for 4:2:0 (frame_crop_right_offset
and frame_crop_bottom_offset of the SPS, which v4l2-h264-enc derives
from the coded size). The overfill only tells the hardware how many
right-most columns to fill itself instead of reading them. With a crop
that isn't a multiple of 4 the last columns are read from the source
buffer, which spans whole macroblocks, and are cropped away by the SPS.
Rockchip's MPP does the same: it programs the overfill as the 4 pixel
part of the padding and crops to any even width.

Round the H.264 crop rectangle to 2 pixels in both directions. Heights
were accepted unrounded, and for an odd height the integer division of
the SPS crop offset made the decoded picture one line taller, so round
them up to 2 as well.
JPEG keeps the 4 pixel rounding.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/verisilicon/hantro_v4l2.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/verisilicon/hantro_v4l2.c b/drivers/media/platform/verisilicon/hantro_v4l2.c
index 8a2702d31b60..40487ee632d4 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/verisilicon/hantro_v4l2.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/verisilicon/hantro_v4l2.c
@@ -868,6 +868,16 @@ static int vidioc_s_selection(struct file *file, void *priv,
 		rect->top = 0;
 		rect->width = ctx->src_fmt.width;
 		rect->height = ctx->src_fmt.height;
+	} else if (ctx->vpu_dst_fmt->codec_mode == HANTRO_MODE_H264_ENC) {
+		/*
+		 * H.264 crops in units of 2 luma samples for 4:2:0 (the SPS
+		 * frame_crop_*_offset). The right overfill register counts 4
+		 * pixel units, so a 2 pixel crop is not filled by the hardware:
+		 * those source columns are read from the buffer, which spans
+		 * whole macroblocks, and fall outside the cropped picture.
+		 */
+		rect->width = round_up(rect->width, 2);
+		rect->height = round_up(rect->height, 2);
 	} else {
 		/* We support widths aligned to 4 pixels and arbitrary heights. */
 		rect->width = round_up(rect->width, 4);
-- 
